WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.647
As environments grow more complex, detection engineering becomes increasingly important.

2
00:00:05.647 --> 00:00:14.428
Organizations need maintainable detections, reliable telemetry, strong documentation, meaningful metrics, and effective collaboration.

3
00:00:14.428 --> 00:00:23.028
Cloud services, SaaS platforms, identity systems, endpoint tooling, applications, and data pipelines all change quickly.

4
00:00:23.028 --> 00:00:27.698
Detection programs must adapt without losing control of quality or ownership.

5
00:00:27.698 --> 00:00:32.078
The future of detection engineering is not just more alerts or more tools.

6
00:00:32.078 --> 00:00:40.200
It is better visibility, clearer context, stronger lifecycle management, and more disciplined improvement based on operational evidence.

7
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:47.733
Automation and AI can help with parts of the work, such as summarization, enrichment, review support, or test generation.

8
00:00:47.733 --> 00:00:55.436
Human judgment remains essential for understanding business context, investigation needs, and acceptable operational tradeoffs.

9
00:00:55.436 --> 00:01:04.356
Detection engineering helps create sustainable defensive capabilities that evolve alongside changing threats, technologies, and business requirements.

10
00:01:04.356 --> 00:01:10.004
The organizations that benefit most will treat detection as a long-term engineering practice.

11
00:01:10.004 --> 00:01:23.533
Future programs will likely place more emphasis on detection portability, structured metadata, testable detection content, coverage mapping, and tighter connections between detection work and incident response lessons.

12
00:01:23.533 --> 00:01:28.782
They will also need stronger partnerships with data engineering and platform teams.

13
00:01:28.782 --> 00:01:38.300
As telemetry volume grows, detection engineers will need reliable pipelines, clear schemas, useful enrichment, and sustainable storage decisions.

14
00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:46.661
Detection engineering is the discipline of designing, building, maintaining, measuring, documenting, and improving security detections.

15
00:01:46.661 --> 00:01:53.366
It transforms telemetry into actionable defensive visibility and relies on collaboration across security teams.

16
00:01:53.366 --> 00:02:03.414
Mature programs use lifecycle management, testing, tuning, documentation, metrics, and continuous improvement to maintain effective defensive capabilities.

17
00:02:03.414 --> 00:02:06.617
Detection engineering is not simply writing alerts.

18
00:02:06.617 --> 00:02:12.314
It is the engineering practice of creating reliable visibility into security-relevant activity.
